ngeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid and the updates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied."}]